[N 37-38 Dungeon: The Drowned City]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Standalone dungeon chapter, played between chapter 34 (Scarlet Monastery) and chapter 35 (Badlands): the optional Troll Witchery and Loremaster Dibbs lead-ins, Krazek's two quests in Booty Bay, one run, and the hand-ins in Booty Bay, Southshore, the Dalaran crater and Ironforge.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  This chapter wants level 37. Krazek's two quests and Timear's idol accept at 34, the Dibbs chain at 30; all the dungeon quests are level 40. Mob levels inside are not in the data (the Wowhead Forever zone page still showed none on 16 Nov; every mob is elite) and the boss loot needs level 33-37. The Skullsplitter Mystics of the optional block are 39-40. Under 37: wait, or go with a group that is 38+
[OC]|cffffffffStandalone|r  -  start in Ironforge, where chapter 34 ends; this chapter ends in Ironforge, where chapter 35 begins. It is on no chain and replaces chapter 31: skip chapter 31. |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, one run, never a re-run. 3,900 quest XP on the one plain quest (The Saltseer Captain), up to 25,100 more on the optional ones (Shady Saltseers 3,900, Ancient Gurubashi Secrets 3,900, the six quests of the Dibbs block 17,300). The hearth is bound in Booty Bay here; chapter 35 moves it to Thelsamar
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r quest ids, objectives and NPC positions from the Forever DB (QuestieDB 1.1.1); drop rates from the Wowhead Forever item pages, read 16 Nov; item stats from the Wowhead Forever tooltips of 16 Nov, scored against the gear worn on 16 Nov. The cave entrance, the layout, the mob levels, where the four tablets stand and whether Deathless Marrow is a boss are not in the data

[OC]|cffffffffLoremaster Dibbs (optional)|r  -  the prize is the |cff66ff66Apprentice Sorcerer's Slacks|r (cloth legs +9 Int +17 Spi +8 spell damage) from The Web of Magic: 68.8 on the weights against the Dark Ritual Leggings at 28.0. It hangs on two luck gates: 4 Skullsplitter Fetishes outside (17.8%, about 22 kills of level 39-40 trolls) and 5 I'lalai Fetishes inside the dungeon (9-17% a kill, 30 to 55 kills of three mob types in the one run - nobody knows whether a run holds that many). It also costs two trips to Southshore. Skip the whole block and go on at the Booty Bay flight step if you do not want it
[OC]|cffffcc00Other legs:|r Depth-Risen Leggings (cloth legs, bind on equip, +17 Spi +10 spell damage) are 62.5 on the weights and drop from the dungeon's trash: look for them on the Ironforge auction house before you decide
